Create Japanese metadata from the audio transcription, optional visual captions, and creator notes. Preserve proper names and requested attribution. Use story context to make the description coherent, not to paste a storyboard or disclose private production notes. For fictional work, describe it as a story rather than historical fact.

Return: title (up to 40 Japanese characters), brief_description (up to 100 characters), middle_description (up to 300 characters), long_description (up to 800 characters), 10 relevant short tags, english_words_to_learn (up to 5 English terms with supported timestamps), teaser (2-4 seconds within the source), cover timestamp, and publish_category. Categories: simplelife for real-life personal recordings; lazyingart for brand/art/product work; musia for song/audio-focused work; lalachan for fictional character stories; lalamv for character or story music videos.

Write descriptions as readable prose. Honor requested credits in each description. Do not invent facts or dialogue absent from the sources.

